================================================================================
                        CUSTOM UI LIBRARY DOCUMENTATION
================================================================================



--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LIBRARY SETUP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The library initializes with a default dark theme and built-in global keybind 
listeners.

Properties:
- Library.Theme (Table): Default color palette.
- Library.Flags (Table): Key-value store of component values keyed by flag name.
- Library.Elements (Table): Component handle references used for programmatically 
  updating state.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WINDOW MANAGEMENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Library:CreateWindow(titleText)
Creates a new draggable and resizable UI window.

local Window = Library:CreateWindow("My Custom Interface")

Window Methods:

- Window:Toggle()
  Toggles the visibility of the main window frame. 
  Returns the new visibility state (boolean).

- Window:isWindowOpen()
  Returns whether the window is currently open (boolean).


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TABS & SUB-SECTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Window:CreateTab(tabName)
Creates a top tab within the window.

local MainTab = Window:CreateTab("Main")

Tab:CreateSubSection(subName)
Creates a visually distinct card/sub-section container inside a tab. Component 
methods can be called directly on the subsection.

local MovementSection = MainTab:CreateSubSection("Movement Features")


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UI COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All components below can be added to a Tab or a SubSection.

--- 1. Button ---
AddButton(text, callback)

MainTab:AddButton("Print Hello", function()
    print("Hello, world!")
end)

--- 2. Toggle ---
AddToggle(text, defaultState, flag, callback)
* Note: flag is optional. If omitted, text will be used as the flag key.

MainTab:AddToggle("WalkSpeed Boost", false, "SpeedToggle", function(state)
    print("Toggle State:", state)
end)

--- 3. Slider ---
AddSlider(text, min, max, default, flag, callback)

MainTab:AddSlider("WalkSpeed", 16, 200, 16, "SpeedSlider", function(value)
    game.Players.LocalPlayer.Character.Humanoid.WalkSpeed = value
end)

--- 4. Keybind ---
AddKeybind(text, defaultKey, flag, callback)
* Accepts Enum.KeyCode or Enum.UserInputType.

MainTab:AddKeybind("Teleport Key", Enum.KeyCode.E, "TPKey", function(key)
    print("Key pressed:", key)
end)

--- 5. Dropdown ---
AddDropdown(text, optionsTable, defaultOption, flag, callback)

MainTab:AddDropdown("Select Mode", {"Mode A", "Mode B", "Mode C"}, "Mode A", "ModeDropdown", function(selected)
    print("Selected option:", selected)
end)

--- 6. Textbox ---
AddTextbox(text, placeholderText, defaultText, flag, callback)
* callback(text, enterPressed): Fires on focus lost.

MainTab:AddTextbox("Custom Name", "Type here...", "Default", "NameTextbox", function(txt, enterPressed)
    print("Submitted text:", txt, "Enter Pressed:", enterPressed)
end)

--- 7. Colorpicker ---
AddColorpicker(text, defaultColor, useAlpha, defaultAlpha, flag, callback)
* Full RGB/HSV picker window with optional alpha channel slider and hexadecimal support.

-- Standard Colorpicker
MainTab:AddColorpicker("Accent Color", Color3.fromRGB(0, 162, 255), false, 1, "AccentPicker", function(color)
    print("Color selected:", color)
end)

-- Colorpicker with Alpha/Opacity
MainTab:AddColorpicker("Box Color", Color3.fromRGB(255, 0, 0), true, 0.5, "BoxColorPicker", function(color, alpha)
    print("Color:", color, "Alpha:", alpha)
end)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The library contains built-in JSON serialization for Color3 and EnumItem types 
using writefile / readfile.

Library:SaveConfig(fileName)
Saves all Library.Flags values into a JSON file in your executor workspace (filename.json).

Library:SaveConfig("my_config")

Library:LoadConfig(fileName)
Loads values from the file and updates all matching UI element states via element:Set(value).

Library:LoadConfig("my_config")

Library:DeleteConfig(fileName)
Deletes the specified config file.

Library:DeleteConfig("my_config")


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THEME SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Library:changeTheme(themeKey, newColor)
Dynamically updates a theme property and updates registered UI elements in real-time.

Valid Theme Keys:
- "Background"
- "Container"
- "ContentBackground"
- "Separator"
- "Accent"
- "Text"
- "MutedText"

Library:changeTheme("Accent", Color3.fromRGB(255, 100, 0))


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMPLETE USAGE EXAMPLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local Library = loadstring(game:HttpGet("YOUR_LIBRARY_URL"))()

local Window = Library:CreateWindow("Control Panel")
local MainTab = Window:CreateTab("General")

local Section = MainTab:CreateSubSection("Player Settings")

Section:AddToggle("Enable Speed", false, "Speed_Toggle", function(enabled)
    print("Speed toggle:", enabled)
end)

Section:AddSlider("Speed Value", 16, 100, 16, "Speed_Value", function(val)
    print("New speed:", val)
end)

Section:AddKeybind("UI Toggle", Enum.KeyCode.RightShift, "UI_Toggle_Key", function()
    Window:Toggle()
end)

local ConfigSection = MainTab:CreateSubSection("Config Manager")

ConfigSection:AddButton("Save Config", function()
    Library:SaveConfig("default")
end)

ConfigSection:AddButton("Load Config", function()
    Library:LoadConfig("default")
end)


AIMBOTLIB------------
- enabled             : (boolean) Master toggle [default: true]
- keybind             : (Enum.KeyCode) Keybind used to activate targeting [default: Enum.KeyCode.E]
- triggerMode         : (string) "Hold" or "Toggle" [default: "Hold"]
- aimMode             : (string) "Mouse" or "Camera" [default: "Mouse"]
- targetSelectionMode : (string) "FOV" or "Distance" [default: "FOV"]
- fovRadius           : (number) Pixel radius for FOV mode [default: 200]
- maxDistance         : (number) Max 3D distance in studs [default: 2000]
- smooth              : (boolean) Enables smooth easing [default: true]
- smoothTime          : (number) Interpolation factor [default: 0.15]
- sensitivity         : (number) Mouse sensitivity multiplier [default: 1]
- targetHitbox        : (string) Target body part [default: "Head"]
- teamCheck           : (boolean) Enable team filtering [default: false]
- checkTeamColor      : (boolean) Check TeamColor equality [default: false]
- targetNeutral       : (boolean) Allow targeting teamless players [default: false]

2. FOV VISUALIZATION SETTINGS
--------------------------------------------------
- showFOV             : (boolean) Show on-screen FOV ring [default: true]
- fovColor            : (Color3) RGB color of the ring [default: 0, 255, 150]
- fovThickness        : (number) Pixel thickness of outline [default: 1.5]
- fovTransparency     : (number) Opacity (0 to 1) [default: 0.7]
- fovFilled           : (boolean) Render filled circle [default: false]

3. PUBLIC METHODS
--------------------------------------------------
- Aimbot:Init()
  Connects RenderStepped and Input listeners. Safe for re-initialization.

- Aimbot:Toggle(state)
  Parameters: state (boolean, optional)
  Toggles or forces active aiming state.

- Aimbot:getClosestPlr()
  Returns: Player or nil
  Evaluates and returns best target based on active selection mode.

- Aimbot:IsEnemy(player)
  Parameters: player (Player)
  Returns: boolean
  Validates player existence, health (>0), and team parameters.

- Aimbot:Destroy()
  Disconnects all events, stops RenderStepped, and cleans up FOV drawings.
